# Machine-local, secret and live pi data.
#
# WARNING: this file has no effect on a machine where ~/.pi is one symlink.
# stow folds a whole folder into a single symlink when the target folder does
# not exist yet. stow then never walks the single files, so it never reads this
# file. Every file under pi/.pi is reachable through ~/.pi, and pi writes its
# live data into this git repository. Only .gitignore keeps that data out of
# your commits.
#
# This file becomes active if ~/.pi ever holds a real file, because stow then
# makes one symlink for each file.
#
# Anchoring rule: stow matches a pattern that holds a "/" against the path
# inside the package WITH a leading slash. Write "^/\.pi/agent/auth\.json$",
# not "^\.pi/agent/auth\.json$" -- the second form can never match. A pattern
# without a "/" is matched against each single name.
#
# This file also replaces the built-in ignore list of stow, so the useful parts
# of that list are repeated at the end.

# Secrets and machine-local settings
^/\.pi/agent/auth\.json$
^/\.pi/agent/settings\.json$
^/\.pi/agent/trust\.json$
^/\.pi/agent/models\.json$

# Live output
^/\.pi/agent/run-history\.jsonl$
^/\.pi/agent/pi-debug\.log$
^/\.pi/agent/sessions(/.*)?$
^/\.pi/agent/npm(/.*)?$

# Build output
node_modules

# Repeated from the built-in list of stow
\.git
\.gitignore
\.gitmodules
\.svn
\.hg
CVS
RCS
_darcs
\.cvsignore
.+~
\#.*\#
\.\#.+
.+,v
^/README.*
^/LICENSE.*
^/COPYING
